WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 064. AN INDUSTRY CAN HAVE RECORDS AND STILL HAVE AMNESIA. Policies, decisions, terminology, corrections, rights, and context can disappear when people leave or systems change.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
USE SYNTHETIC RECORDS. EVENT · POLICY · ACTOR · TERM. No real person, patient, company, agency, law, product, study, or community record appears in this fixed archive.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
BUILD THE MEMORY. RECORD · CONTEXT · SOURCE · CHANGE. Keep each archived object connected to its version, source, context, rights state, correction history, and later change.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
PRESERVE DISAGREEMENT. CURRENT · SUPERSEDED · CONTESTED · RESTRICTED. Do not erase earlier policy, select a winning account, expose restricted material, or invent missing context.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
BOUND THE RESULT. AN ARCHIVE IS NOT AUTHORITY. The demo cannot establish historical truth, current law, medical validity, identity, consent, ownership, cultural permission, or completeness.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. MAKE THE TRAIL SURVIVE TURNOVER. INSTITUTIONAL MEMORY IS USABLE WHEN THE RECORD, CONTEXT, SOURCE, CHANGE, AND LIMIT REMAIN CONNECTED.

